<title>DENMARK: Danish March unemployment falls to 8.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish March unemployment falls to 8.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 8.0 percent of the workforce in March 1997, down from 8.1 percent in February, the National Statistics Office said on Monday.</p>
<p>				 March 1997    Feb 1997   March 1996</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate    8.0 pct	 8.1 pct    *9.1 pct</p>
<p>    Total unemployed     222,400	 225,500    *255,500</p>
<p>*Revised</p>
<p>All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast seasonally adjusted March year-on-year unemployment of 8.0 percent. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652.</p>
</text>
